Here's an idea that just popped into my head.  How about this: When a character
learns a spell they remember it forever, but every time they cast it the 
amount of power they will need to cast it the next time increases slightly.
So a character could cast the spell quite often at first, but eventually it
would take most of their power just to cast it once, and it would take a long
time to regenerate.  If the spell is really overused, the power needed to cast
it would increase to more than the character's max power.  Then they would have
to gain a level or quaff a potion to increase their power somehow.

So what do you think?  This would provide a barrier against casting a spell too
much or too often, but it wouldn't be an insurmountable barrier, like it is
now.

A slight modification: It would be possible to cast spells that have gone
way up in power, but there would be a chance of frying your brain and losing
INT, or a similar penalty.  This would work in conjunction with my first idea.
Obviously, there would be a greater chance of frying your brain if you try to
cast a 100-power spell with only 1 power than if you try to cast it with 75
power.

